{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1417790-question-on-scale-and-durability","id":1417790,"title":"Question on scale and durability","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-12T04:14:37-07:00","id":1417790,"title":"Question on scale and durability","content":"Hello all, just bought all the hardback books for TC and I'm having a hard time with the scaling mechanic.<br /> <br /> The one I have the most problem with is, things that might stack.<br /> <br /> Ex. Scarab strike frigate: size 4, tag: massive 2<br /> <br /> So does this effect the defense value twice?<br /> Increase in size +2 and enhanced durability +2?<br /> <br /> With the size already giving it +3 defense, that brings the total defense upto +7.<br /> <br /> Am I right in this thought?<br /> <br /> Additionally would the massive tag affect the weapon systems giving them a +4?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","user":"cKnight","date":".  Added a question 10-12-2020, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T04:43:57-07:00","id":1417793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1417790-question-on-scale-and-durability#post1417790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all, just bought all the hardback books for TC and I'm having a hard time with the scaling mechanic.<br /> <br /> The one I have the most problem with is, things that might stack.<br /> <br /> Ex. Scarab strike frigate: size 4, tag: massive 2<br /> <br /> So does this effect the defense value twice?<br /> Increase in size +2 and enhanced durability +2?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the size is consequence of the tag, not addition to that. A ship is size 2 +1 per massive tag.<br /> <br /> Scale don\u2019t stack, in this case Size scale turns into durability scale to that end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With the size already giving it +3 defense, that brings the total defense upto +7.<br /> <br /> Am I right in this thought? </div> </div> </div>No, size don\u2019t give defense, it gives durability. It\u2019s not hard to hit the ship, it\u2019s hard to deal damage to it. The easiest way to do so is by saying it increases the defense by 2 per scale, but if you what to paint the ship with a paintball pistol, the defense is not affected, same for a Quantakinetic trying to touch it for some reason.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the defense of the ship against a Size 1 attacker will be 7 (1 base + 6, twice the size difference). But a scale 4 weapon will be at same scale, so the defense will be 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Additionally would the massive tag affect the weapon systems giving them a +4? </div> </div> </div>Scale don\u2019t work that way, scale work in the difference between the 2 sides envolved. A ship with the Weaponry 2 tag have weapons the same scale as it, so, against humans, the ship would gain +6 enhancements and will be able to cause 3 additional injuries in the target, besides the first and critical ones. But when fighting another ship it will be as neither had scale, as both are the same scale.<br /> <br /> Now, ships may have different size weapons, Weaponry 1 tag gives weapons scale equal to \u00bd of the ship size scale round up, in this case scale 2. When attacking a size 4 ship with those weapons, the attacker will suffer +4 in the difficulty of the attack, as the weapons are 2 scales bellow the target scale.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T18:24:53-07:00","id":1417966,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the clarification. I just reread through the vehicle section of core and aeon. I get it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}